# PART 7 — Payment Events & Webhook Processing

This is a **major backend milestone** for RevRecover.

After Part 6, you had:

```text
Razorpay
   ↓
Webhook
   ↓
Signature verification
```

After Part 7, you'll have:

```text
Razorpay
   │
   │ payment.failed
   ▼
POST /webhooks/razorpay
   │
   ├── verify raw-body signature
   │
   ├── validate event
   │
   ├── identify Razorpay event ID
   │
   ├── identify organisation
   │
   ├── persist webhook_events
   │
   ├── idempotency protection
   │
   └── process event
            │
            ▼
         Payment
            │
            ▼
      PaymentAttempt
            │
            ▼
     domain event
            │
            ▼
      Future recovery
```

Razorpay uses **at-least-once webhook delivery**, so duplicate deliveries are expected. The `x-razorpay-event-id` header is unique per event and is specifically intended to help with deduplication. Razorpay also warns that webhook events may arrive out of order. ([Razorpay][1])

We will therefore make idempotency a **database constraint**, not merely:

```python
if event_exists:
    ...
```

because that has a race condition.

---

# 1. Branch

From the repository root:

```powershell
cd D:\RevRecover

git status

git checkout main
git pull

git checkout -b feature/payment-events
```

Verify:

```powershell
git branch
```

You should see:

```text
* feature/payment-events
  main
```

