# 81. Testing without Razorpay

Before connecting a real Razorpay webhook, generate a local signed payload.

PowerShell:

```powershell
$body = @'
{
  "entity": "event",
  "account_id": "acc_test123",
  "event": "payment.failed",
  "contains": ["payment"],
  "payload": {
    "payment": {
      "entity": {
        "id": "pay_test123",
        "amount": 450000,
        "currency": "INR",
        "status": "failed",
        "order_id": "order_test123",
        "email": "customer@example.com",
        "contact": "9999999999",
        "error": {
          "code": "BAD_REQUEST_ERROR",
          "description": "Payment failed"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "created_at": 1777440000
}
'@
```

Use the exact current Unix timestamp when testing replay logic; don't copy the example timestamp blindly.

---

# 82. Generate signature

```powershell
$secret = "your_webhook_secret"

$hmac = [System.Security.Cryptography.HMACSHA256]::new(
    [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($secret)
)

$signature = -join (
    $hmac.ComputeHash(
        [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($body)
    ) | ForEach-Object {
        $_.ToString("x2")
    }
)

$signature
```

---

# 83. Send webhook

```powershell
$eventId = "evt_test_payment_failed_001"

Invoke-RestMethod `
    -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:8000/webhooks/razorpay" `
    -Method Post `
    -Headers @{
        "X-Razorpay-Signature" = $signature
        "X-Razorpay-Event-Id" = $eventId
    } `
    -ContentType "application/json" `
    -Body $body
```

Expected:

```json
{
  "received": true,
  "duplicate": false,
  "event_id": "evt_test_payment_failed_001"
}
```

---

# 84. Send it again

Run the exact command again.

Expected:

```json
{
  "received": true,
  "duplicate": true,
  "event_id": "evt_test_payment_failed_001"
}
```

This is your first real idempotency test.

