# 104. One important thing before Part 8

**Part 8 should NOT immediately jump into the Recovery Engine.**

We need one infrastructure layer first:

# PART 8 — Background Jobs

Branch:

```text
feature/background-jobs
```

Architecture:

```text
Razorpay
   ↓
Webhook
   ↓
Verify
   ↓
webhook_events
   ↓
HTTP 200
   ↓
Redis
   ↓
Celery Worker
   ↓
process_razorpay_webhook
   ↓
Payment
   ↓
PaymentAttempt
   ↓
PaymentFailedEvent
```

This is important because Razorpay's current guidance explicitly recommends immediate acknowledgement and asynchronous processing, and Razorpay retries failed/non-2xx deliveries. ([Razorpay][4])

### Before you ask for Part 8, send me these existing files

Because Part 8 needs to integrate with your **actual current backend**, rather than me guessing your infrastructure:

```text
backend/app/main.py
backend/app/core/config.py
backend/app/db/database.py
backend/app/db/init_db.py
backend/app/models/__init__.py

backend/app/api/webhooks/razorpay.py

backend/app/models/payment.py
backend/app/models/customer.py
backend/app/models/organisation.py
backend/app/models/organisation_member.py
backend/app/models/system.py

backend/requirements.txt
backend/.env.example
```

Also send your current:

```text
app/api/payments/repository.py
app/api/payments/service.py
```

**if those files exist in your current Part 5 implementation.**

Don't send any real Razorpay secrets.

Use:

```env
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=<redacted>
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=<redacted>
